                <pb facs="0422" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg398"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Federal Council to Mr. Fogg.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 30, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Not having yet up to this time received answer to the note which it had the honor
                    to address the 3d July, 1883, to the minister resident of the United States of
                    America, concerning contributions in favor of the family of Jean Zweifel, the
                    federal council thinks it ought to remind Mr. George G. Fogg of this affair, and
                    seizes this occasion to renew to him the assurances, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DR. J. DUBS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
